[Fact:musicEn:Leftover "@Music.en"]
The nine bytes at #R$728E to #N$7296 are the leftover filename
<code>@Music.en</code> at the end of the menu-music source block
(#R$6F04). #R$AAB3 copies those bytes to #N$FFF6 with the rest of the block.
Nothing in the game prints or otherwise uses the string.

[Fact:trapdoorHeader:Tape header remnant]
#R$5F65 to #N$5F6E hold the ten-character tape header name
<code>TRAPDOOR</code> (padded with spaces) left by the loader. The bytes sit
in otherwise unused memory between the system variables and the display
buffers.

[Fact:yourre:YOUR'RE]
The Bad Tempered Thing aside at #R$DD09 stores
<code>YOUR'RE ON YOUR OWN</code>. That is presumably meant to read
<code>YOU'RE ON YOUR OWN</code>. The typo is in the original game, so the
bytes are left exactly as they are.

[Fact:imUpstairs:'IM]
The aside at #R$DD42 stores <code>'IM UPSTAIRS WAITS</code>. That is
presumably meant to read <code>I'M UPSTAIRS WAITS</code>. The typo is in the
original game, so the bytes are left exactly as they are.

[Fact:learnerSuper:Learner Berk / Super Berk]
#R$72A9 is the Learner Berk mode flag. The main-menu chooser at #R$F43D
writes #N$00 for Super Berk (#CHR$53) or #N$01 for Learner Berk (#CHR$4C).
Readers include #R$AC07, #R$AC55, #R$AC7D, #R$AEB2, #R$AF5E, #R$BC12 and
#R$DE19.
